n of the teacher in Rashi.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The proposal of two figures occurs explicitly in the checked Tosafot. It remains the commentary’s proposal.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"This text explicitly juxtaposes Yirmeyah bar Vav and Yose on majorities.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The father’s notice cites the exact Bavli variant in Rav’s statement. The parallel alternative there is Aḥa, the brother of Abba.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"R. Abba addresses Rav Yirmeyah as mar while he is examining the sinews.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The chain is explicit in the Megillah discussion, where Rav follows as the original authority.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Shabbat attests the chain Avina, Yirmeyah, then Rav.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yirmeyah and Giddel’s transmission is explicit. This is the first of two separate references to this face.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The relevant preceding subject is the teacher discussion and its named versions. Tosafot argues for the relation from Ulla’s description.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Berakhot and Eruvin name Mari as son of Rav Huna, son of Yirmeyah bar Abba.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Bava Kamma establishes the transmission. Levi is Huna bar Ḥiyya’s son, and the Chullin and Shabbat reports identify his maternal grandfather as Yirmeyah.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"R. Zeira transmits the rule in the name of Yirmeyah, who cites Shemuel in the checked passage.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"R. Zeira gives the explicit wording about the daytime fast. Distinguish Ḥisda’s statement immediately before it.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Ḥisda transmits the explanation of Psalm 91.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"A series on the kings, the four groups and Psalm 91 bears this transmission.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Ḥisda gives the teaching about labor on a fast day.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yehudah transmits the teaching about Nebuchadnezzar.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Yehudah transmits a joint statement of Rav and Shemuel through Yirmeyah.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"This occurrence explicitly transmits R. Yoḥanan on facial features.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"R. Abba transmits Yirmeyah in Rav’s name.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The first form identifies the teacher as Rav; the second has Rav name Rabbi Yehudah HaNasi as his own teacher.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The first chain runs to Rav; the adjacent alternative runs via Rav to Rabbi.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Rava transmits the stepmother interpretation.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Rava transmits Rav’s three-month ruling through Yirmeyah. This witness uses Rav for Yirmeyah.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The text expressly leaves Rav and Shemuel as alternatives.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The related local notice explicitly discusses the student claim and distinguishes the reported Rabbah attribution.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The cited discussions explicitly identify the maternal grandfather.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The transfer to Yirmeyah at Shum Tamya is explicit. Rashbam glosses it as a place name.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The attribution to Rav concerns measuring flour on the festival.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Ḥullin has this chain. The parallel local Yirmeyah bar Taḥlifa notice draws the distinction explicitly.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The checked talmudic chain is explicit in the Niddah discussion.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The same Sheshet–Yirmeyah exchange asks whether Rav stated his teaching in accordance with the Kutim, reading ככותאי rather than the printed כוותאי. The subject of the teaching is Rav. Preserve both forms and identify the speaker from the explicit context.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Tosafot reports these copy readings. The checked Bavli has Rabbi in Berakhot and Rav in the named Kiddushin passage. The historical set of copies remains uncollated.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The checked printed digital edition has Yose in the passage. Keep the parenthetical Assi identification as the source’s proposed reading.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Pesachim verifies the visit but does not supply this inquiry. Keep the bare report pending a primary passage.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Ḥanan notice repeats the same meeting, but it gives no exact underlying citation. Preserve the report as stated.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Berakhot 27b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_27b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Berakhot 27a:15","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Berakhot_27a.15"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Eruvin 40b:14","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Eruvin_40b.14"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Pesachim 106b:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Pesachim_106b.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Pesachim 106b:3:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Pesachim_106b.3.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 46a:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_46a.1"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Kiddushin 45b:11","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Kiddushin_45b.11"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Tosafot on Kiddushin 46a:1:1","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Tosafot_on_Kiddushin_46a.1.1"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"},{"reference":"Jerusalem Talmud Ketubot 1:10:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Jerusalem_Talmud_Ketubot_1.10.4"},"witness":"The Jerusalem Talmud